# Backend

Follow `docs/coding-standards-backend.md`.

- Typed public functions (`-> None` if needed). `list[T]`, `X | None` — not `List`/`Optional`.
- `from typing import Annotated` for FastAPI `Depends`. `IntegrityError` comes from `sqlalchemy.exc`.
- Keyword-only ids: `user_id=`, `team_id=`. No mutable defaults. No `Any` in domain code.
- Pydantic in `schemas`, ORM in `models`, `StrEnum` on the wire (persist `.value`, not member name), `uuid.UUID` for ids.
- `async def` for I/O only. Services raise domain errors; never `None` for "not allowed".
- Routers → services → repositories. Get-or-create; unique `(team, date)` and completions.
- Team timezone for "today". Error body `{ "error": { "code", "message" } }`.
- No individual rankings. Do not log tokens, passwords, or private reflections.
